## First principles

- **Memory vs. knowledge**: this store holds both. Memory is
  compressed — summaries and indexes. Knowledge is the
  detailed layer below. Any category that admits detailed
  notes still needs an `index.md` that summarizes its
  contents — the categories list above tells you which
  those are by reading their `_guides.md`.
- **Cross-project only**: anything tied to a single project
  belongs in that project's memory bank, not here. The
  project-summary category in this vault exists to make the
  vault discoverable from any project, not to hold project-
  local detail.
- **Optimize for the agent, not the human**: structure, indexes,
  and consistent naming matter more than prose. The human
  benefit is a side effect.
